<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Ho et al. (2019) & Painter, Ho & Headon (2018) avian feather tracts on a curved trunk-and-limb surface: geodesic EDA competence wave, inhibitory-disk hexagonal packing, density-threshold tract boundaries and curvature-induced 5-7 dislocations — Model fidelity to source: 91/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Implements the Painter, Ho & Headon (2018) Keller-Segel n/c/b system with its exact linear threshold chi_c = 0.0540 (L167-229) and lifts it to a curved skin surface: Monge-patch metric, sqrt(det g), g^{ij} and Gaussian curvature (L314-372), a conservative face-flux Laplace-Beltrami / surface chemotaxis operator (L374-399), a Godunov eikonal geodesic EDA competence wave (L401-435) and the Ho 2019 mesenchymal density threshold n_0(1 + gamma t) >= n_crit with n_crit set by the measured margin densities 49 / 66 / 98 cells per 100 um (L548-749). Tract-boundary dislocations between the dorsal and limb tracts are now a mechanistic consequence of curvature (Lean Theorems 4-6; Bausch 2003), closing the v2 remediation item. Scored below v2's 94 because primordium nucleation is a wave-gated inhibitory-disk adsorption rule relaxed by the PDE rather than an emergent PDE instability (`model_boundary_note` in the reference JSON), the eikonal solver uses only the diagonal metric, and the limb-bud geometry is schematic." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "datasets/avian_feather_bud_hexagonal/avian_feather_bud_hexagonal_reference.json L1–L259: governing_equations.model_boundary_note states nucleation is not emergent from the PDE; curved_surface_model.limitations lists the diagonal-metric eikonal and schematic limb geometry <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/datasets/avian_feather_bud_hexagonal/avian_feather_bud_hexagonal_reference.json#L1-L259>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-model-fidelity-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-model-fidelity-5> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Ho et al. (2019) & Painter, Ho & Headon (2018) avian feather tracts on a curved trunk-and-limb surface: geodesic EDA competence wave, inhibitory-disk hexagonal packing, density-threshold tract boundaries and curvature-induced 5-7 dislocations — Morphometric validation: 93/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1304-1422) emits 16 measurements with method, reference and uncertainty notes: Delta_x / lambda_y = 0.866, chi_c = 0.054, WT P_6 = 1.00 (ref 0.75), simultaneous P_6 = 0.69 (ref 0.50), Fc-chEDA1 width 1.25x, Ecto-D2 0.50x, MTX + Ecto-D2 / min(single) = 0.53 (< 1 as in Fig 5F), 0-bud negative controls, specimen count 24 and P_6 = 0.75, curved vs flat three-tract P_6 (0.905 vs 0.979), curved/flat-region defect-fraction ratio 2.81 (null 1.0), limb-height sweep pairs 10 at A_l = 45 (0 at A_l = 0), sphere disclination charge 12 (exact), isochrone-lemma violations 0, dorsal-femoral apterium gap 1.19 lambda. Three width ratios carry `reference_value: null` because Ho 2019 does not tabulate them (only ordering / significance), and the WT model lattice is noise-free so its P_6 = 1.00 exceeds the paper's ~0.75; both are stated explicitly." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-measurement-bare-inter-tract-apterium-gap-between-dorsal-and-femoral-tracts-curved-surface>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-measurement-critical-fgf20-chemotactic-sensitivity-threshold-chi-c>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-measurement-curved-trunk-limb-bud-surface-three-tract-p-6-vs-flat-three-tract-control>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-measurement-defect-fraction-in-curved-k-k-thr-vs-flat-k-k-thr-regions-of-the-curved-surface>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-measurement-ecto-d2-n-crit-98-66-patterned-region-width-ratio-to-control>,
