<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-overall> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Ho et al. (2019) & Painter, Ho & Headon (2018) avian feather tracts on a curved trunk-and-limb surface: geodesic EDA competence wave, inhibitory-disk hexagonal packing, density-threshold tract boundaries and curvature-induced 5-7 dislocations — MorphoEval overall 91.8/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `2018-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal.py`. The script now solves the Painter, Ho & Headon (2018) dermal chemotaxis + FGF20 / BMP PDE on a 3D Monge-patch trunk with four limb buds (Laplace-Beltrami operator, geodesic eikonal EDA competence wave, 3D chordal inhibitory-disk nucleation, local tangent-plane Delaunay coordination) and adds the Ho et al. (2019) mesenchymal density threshold, so the dorsal, humeral and femoral tracts self-delimit through bare apteria (gap 1.19 lambda) and acquire curvature-induced 5-7 dislocations where the limb buds bend the sheet (flat P_6 = 0.979, 0 pairs -> curved P_6 = 0.905, 7 pairs; defect fraction 0.222 at |K| > K_thr vs 0.079 elsewhere; monotone in limb height; sphere disclination charge 12). The flat-sheet suite reproduces the Ho 2019 ordering: WT wave P_6 = 1.00 vs simultaneous (Latrunculin-paused) 0.69 (paper ~0.75 vs ~0.50); Fc-chEDA1 (n_crit = 49/66) widens the patterned region 1.25x, Ecto-D2 (98/66) narrows it to 0.50x, MTX 0.75x, MTX + Ecto-D2 0.26x (< each single treatment); scaleless / Latrunculin give 0 buds. Specimen segmentation of Ho 2019 Fig 3 is unchanged (24 primordia, P_6 = 0.75, +48h/+24h = 2.11x). Provenance was corrected: the Pass 1-2 seed citation (Glimm 2014) is fabricated and has been removed from the bib, JSON, README and docstring; Ho 2019's title and Michon 2008's venue/DOI were fixed; all five DOIs were Crossref-verified. Six Lean 4 theorems (0 sorrys) back the dispersion threshold, hexagonal equidistance, wave fidelity advantage, Euler disclination charge, isochrone row-count dislocation and Monge-metric determinant. Overall 91.8/100 (faithfulness 92.2, reproducibility 90.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 91, Morphological realism / specimen match 92, Parameter expressivity 94, Morphometric validation 93, Source and data traceability 86, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 94. Output judged: docs/media/avian_feather_bud_hexagonal_comparison.png: rendered output of 2018-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal.py at d58a084, image/png, 1618568 B, 2934×2025 px, artifact_sha256 ba009d31e0385026103342b2010994117e85753b24af6da1eb9e321c9ab2511d (sha256 ba009d31e0385026103342b2010994117e85753b24af6da1eb9e321c9ab2511d), spec_fingerprint 3fbee933f34698c1174f68ad05c98568d7506c7ded5d60e6139c6071b4be189e. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 3fbee933f34698c1174f68ad05c98568d7506c7ded5d60e6139c6071b4be189e; artifact_sha256: ba009d31e0385026103342b2010994117e85753b24af6da1eb9e321c9ab2511d; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/avian_feather_bud_hexagonal/avian_feather_bud_hexagonal_reference.json=61c579212066cfb2..., datasets/avian_feather_bud_hexagonal/chick_feather_bud_hexagonal_specimen.jpg=ce18b1c0e01ecb20..., datasets/avian_feather_bud_hexagonal/paper_citations.bib=721ac5198ac62b2d..., datasets/avian_feather_bud_hexagonal/scout_manifest.json=1ff38c1e609c69ea...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-audit-v2." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Digitise the Ho et al. (2019) Fig 3E / 3G / 5F bar values (S-data) to give the Fc-chEDA1, Ecto-D2 and MTX width ratios real reference values and a calibrated mesenchymal density gradient (n_base, L_dens), and add measured noise so the WT model P_6 lands near the paper's ~0.75 rather than the ideal 1.00.",
        "remediation needed: Make primordium nucleation emergent: replace the wave-gated inhibitory-disk adsorption rule in `simulate_feather_array_on_surface` by condensation arising from the surface Keller-Segel PDE itself, using an upwind / flux-limited discretisation of div_g(n grad_g c) on the Monge patch (the centred scheme was checkerboard-unstable in Pass 3), and re-derive P_6, tract widths and curvature defects from the emergent condensates.",
        "remediation needed: Regenerate `scout_manifest.json` from a fresh literature scout so it no longer records the fabricated Glimm 2014 seed (re-pin its SHA-256), and rename the script / sim_id away from the 'glimm' token once the audit chain can be re-keyed.",
        "remediation needed: Replace the schematic Gaussian limb-bud Monge patch with a surface digitised from a staged chick embryo (e.g. Ho et al. 2019 Fig 1B whole mount or an HH29-30 3D atlas), solve the eikonal equation with the full (off-diagonal) metric, and evaluate per-tract Gauss-Bonnet with the boundary geodesic-curvature term so tract disclination charges can be compared quantitatively, not just by sign." ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.18e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-parameter-expressivity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Ho et al. (2019) & Painter, Ho & Headon (2018) avian feather tracts on a curved trunk-and-limb surface: geodesic EDA competence wave, inhibitory-disk hexagonal packing, density-threshold tract boundaries and curvature-induced 5-7 dislocations — Parameter expressivity: 94/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
