<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-specimen-match> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Ho et al. (2019) & Painter, Ho & Headon (2018) avian feather tracts on a curved trunk-and-limb surface: geodesic EDA competence wave, inhibitory-disk hexagonal packing, density-threshold tract boundaries and curvature-induced 5-7 dislocations — Morphological realism / specimen match: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Vendors and SHA-256-verifies Ho et al. (2019) PLOS Biology 17(2):e3000132 Fig 3 (`chick_feather_bud_hexagonal_specimen.jpg`, CC BY 4.0) and segments it (`segment_feather_tract_specimen`, L971-1025): 24 CTNNB1 / EDA primordia in Panel B ROI [494, 24, 770, 218] with Voronoi / Delaunay coordination P_6 = 0.7500 (9/12 interior), P_567 = 1.0, |psi_6| = 0.5265, NN spacing 40.33 +- 7.96 px (CV 0.1974), and the Panel A +24h -> +48h tract expansion 38 / 18 = 2.11x. The comparison figure (Panels G-H, L1172-1190) now sets the specimen against the correct Ho 2019 anchors (P_6 ~0.75 control vs ~0.50 Latrunculin-paused) instead of the invented v2 value 0.9167. Held at 92: the curved trunk + limb-bud surface is a schematic Monge patch, not segmented from an embryo image, so the new curved-tract outputs are compared to flat controls and to theory, not to a specimen." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
