<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Painter, Ho & Headon (2018) Keller-Segel / FGF20 Dermal Chemotactic Instability vs. Scaleless (sc/sc) Stability" ;
    dct:description "Proves that supercritical FGF20 chemotaxis (χ > χ_c) drives spontaneous dermal mesenchymal condensation (det_KS < 0), whereas FGF20 loss in the scaleless (sc/sc) mutant or Latrunculin motility blockade (χ = 0) guarantees uniform dermal stability (det_KS > 0). In the Pass 3 code the same χ_c gates the nucleation rule (chi < CHI_CRITICAL => no primordia). | Variables: n(x,t): dermal mesenchymal cell density; c(x,t): FGF20 chemoattractant; χ: chemotactic sensitivity; D_n, D_c: diffusivities; q = k^2: squared spatial wavenumber" ;
    dct:source "Painter, Ho & Headon (2018) J. Theor. Biol. 437:225-238 Section 2-3; Ho et al. (2019) PLoS Biol. 17(2):e3000132 Fig 1C, S5 Fig" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2018-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal.py#L167-L229>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_019_avian_feather_bud_hexagonal.lean#L29-L48> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def keller_segel_fgf20_det (D_n r_n D_c mu_c chi n_0 f_c q : Int) : Int :=
  (D_n * q + r_n) * (D_c * q + mu_c) - chi * n_0 * f_c * q
def scaleless_neg_trace (D_n D_c r_n mu_c q : Nat) : Nat :=
  (D_n + D_c) * q + (r_n + 1) + (mu_c + 1)
def scaleless_pos_det (Dq_prod D_n_mu D_c_r r_pos : Nat) : Nat :=
  Dq_prod + D_n_mu + D_c_r + (r_pos + 1)
theorem keller_segel_fgf20_chemotactic_instability (D_n D_c r_n mu_c q Dq_prod D_n_mu D_c_r r_pos : Nat) :
    scaleless_neg_trace D_n D_c r_n mu_c q ≥ 2 ∧
    scaleless_pos_det Dq_prod D_n_mu D_c_r r_pos ≥ r_pos + 1 ∧
    keller_segel_fgf20_det 1 1 1 2 0 1 3 1 = 6 ∧
    keller_segel_fgf20_det 1 1 1 2 1 1 3 1 = 3 ∧
    keller_segel_fgf20_det 1 1 1 2 4 1 3 1 = -6 := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, by decide, by decide, by decide⟩
  · simp [scaleless_neg_trace]; omega
  · simp [scaleless_pos_det]
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "det_KS(q) = (D_n q + r_n)(D_c q + μ_c) - χ n_0 f_c q < 0  (χ > χ_c),   det_KS(q)|_{χ=0} = (D_n q + r_n)(D_c q + μ_c) > 0  ∀ q > 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2017.10.026>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1081160>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.018341>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.3000132>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.3000448> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Keller-Segel Dermal Chemotaxis + FGF20/BMP Lateral Inhibition behind a Geodesic EDA Competence Wave on a Curved Monge-Patch Skin Surface with Density-Threshold Tract Boundaries (Painter, Ho & Headon 2018; Ho et al. 2019; Bausch et al. 2003)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_019.keller_segel_fgf20_det" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_019.keller_segel_fgf20_chemotactic_instability" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Equilateral Row-to-Row Half-Phase Offset & 6-Equidistant Nearest-Neighbor Theorem (Ho et al. 2019 Fig 3B lattice)" ;
    dct:description "Proves that when lateral inhibition pins each successive mediolateral row at half-period offset Δy = λ_y / 2 and spacing Δx = (√3/2) λ_y, all 6 nearest neighbours lie at identical distance λ_y (60° hexagonal array). Used by the primary-row / inhibitory-disk nucleation geometry and by the flat-sheet P_6 = 1.0 control. | Variables: λ_y: longitudinal intra-row feather bud spacing; Δy = λ_y / 2: inhibitor-pinned half-period phase offset; Δx: mediolateral inter-row spacing" ;
    dct:source "Ho et al. (2019) PLoS Biol. 17:e3000132 Fig 3B, Fig 2A; Painter, Ho & Headon (2018) J. Theor. Biol. 437:225-238 Fig 5" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2018-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal.py#L231-L312>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_019_avian_feather_bud_hexagonal.lean#L63-L74> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def scaled_inter_row_diag_dist_sq (dx_sq ly_sq : Int) : Int :=
  4 * dx_sq + ly_sq
def scaled_intra_row_dist_sq (ly_sq : Int) : Int :=
  4 * ly_sq
theorem hexagonal_row_offset_equidistance (dx_sq ly_sq : Int)
    (h_hex : 4 * dx_sq = 3 * ly_sq) :
    scaled_inter_row_diag_dist_sq dx_sq ly_sq = scaled_intra_row_dist_sq ly_sq := by
  simp [scaled_inter_row_diag_dist_sq, scaled_intra_row_dist_sq]
  omega
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "d_diag^2 = (Δx)^2 + (λ_y / 2)^2 = λ_y^2  ⟺  4(Δx)^2 = 3 λ_y^2  ⟺  Δx = (√3 / 2) λ_y ≈ 0.8660 λ_y" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2017.10.026>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1081160>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.018341>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.3000132>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.3000448> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Keller-Segel Dermal Chemotaxis + FGF20/BMP Lateral Inhibition behind a Geodesic EDA Competence Wave on a Curved Monge-Patch Skin Surface with Density-Threshold Tract Boundaries (Painter, Ho & Headon 2018; Ho et al. 2019; Bausch et al. 2003)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_019.scaled_inter_row_diag_dist_sq" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_019.hexagonal_row_offset_equidistance" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Ho et al. (2019) & Bailleul et al. (2019) Traveling Competence Wave Hexagonal Fidelity Enhancement Theorem" ;
    dct:description "Proves that sequential row-by-row competence propagation achieves strictly higher hexagonal fidelity P_6 than simultaneous whole-tract competence (Ho 2019 Fig 2D: ~75 % vs ~50 % six-sided Voronoi cells, control vs Latrunculin-paused explants). Pass 3 corrects the attribution: the simultaneous regime is the Latrunculin-pause/release experiment, not Fc-chEDA1. | Variables: v_w: mediolateral EDA competence wave speed; P_6: percentage of 6-coordinated Voronoi polygons; d_min: intrinsic defect floor; d_gain: simultaneous-nucleation grain-boundary defect penalty" ;
    dct:source "Ho et al. (2019) PLoS Biol. 17(2):e3000132 Fig 2B-D, Fig 4; Bailleul et al. (2019) PLoS Biol. 17(10):e3000448" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2018-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal.py#L844-L912>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_019_avian_feather_bud_hexagonal.lean#L89-L103> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def hexagonal_p6_opt_pct (d_min : Nat) : Nat :=
  100 - d_min
def hexagonal_p6_simul_pct (d_min d_gain : Nat) : Nat :=
  100 - (d_min + (d_gain + 1))
theorem traveling_wave_hexagonal_fidelity_advantage (d_min d_gain : Nat)
    (h_bound : d_min + (d_gain + 1) ≤ 100) :
    hexagonal_p6_opt_pct d_min > hexagonal_p6_simul_pct d_min d_gain ∧
    hexagonal_p6_opt_pct 8 = 92 ∧
    hexagonal_p6_simul_pct 8 41 = 50 := by
  refine ⟨?_, by decide, by decide⟩
  simp [hexagonal_p6_opt_pct, hexagonal_p6_simul_pct]
  omega
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "P_6(v_opt) = 100 - d_min > P_6(v → ∞) = 100 - (d_min + d_gain)  (d_gain ≥ 1);   P_6(v_opt) = 92% > P_6(v → ∞) = 50%" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2017.10.026>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1081160>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.018341>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.3000132>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.3000448> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Keller-Segel Dermal Chemotaxis + FGF20/BMP Lateral Inhibition behind a Geodesic EDA Competence Wave on a Curved Monge-Patch Skin Surface with Density-Threshold Tract Boundaries (Painter, Ho & Headon 2018; Ho et al. 2019; Bausch et al. 2003)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_019.hexagonal_p6_opt_pct" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_019.traveling_wave_hexagonal_fidelity_advantage" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Euler / Gauss-Bonnet Disclination Charge of a Closed Triangulated Primordium Lattice (Bausch et al. 2003)" ;
    dct:description "Proves that Gaussian curvature forces 5-/7-coordinated defects into the hexagonal feather lattice independent of the primordium positions: on the curved limb-bud flanks the humeral and femoral tracts must dislocate. Checked numerically by sphere_topological_charge_check() (charge 12 on a Fibonacci sphere) and used by curvature_defect_analysis() to localise 5-7 pairs where |K| > K_thr. | Variables: V, E, F: vertices (primordia), edges, triangular faces of the Delaunay lattice; z_i: coordination number; χ: Euler characteristic; n_5, n_7: five- and seven-coordinated primordia" ;
    dct:source "Bausch et al. (2003) Science 299(5613):1716-1718; Ho et al. (2019) PLoS Biol. 17:e3000132 Fig 1B (tracts on the curved trunk and limbs)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2018-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal.py#L437-L546>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_019_avian_feather_bud_hexagonal.lean#L119-L133> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def disclination_charge (V sum_z : Int) : Int :=
  6 * V - sum_z
theorem euler_disclination_charge (V E F sum_z : Int)
    (h_faces : 3 * F = 2 * E) (h_degrees : sum_z = 2 * E) :
    disclination_charge V sum_z = 6 * (V - E + F) := by
  simp [disclination_charge]
  omega
theorem sphere_pentagon_excess (n5 n6 n7 E F : Int)
    (h_faces : 3 * F = 2 * E)
    (h_degrees : 5 * n5 + 6 * n6 + 7 * n7 = 2 * E)
    (h_euler : (n5 + n6 + n7) - E + F = 2) :
    n5 - n7 = 12 := by
  omega
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "Σ_i (6 - z_i) = 6V - Σ z_i = 6(V - E + F) = 6χ   (3F = 2E, Σ z_i = 2E);   sphere: n_5 - n_7 = 12" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2017.10.026>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1081160>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.018341>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.3000132>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.3000448> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Keller-Segel Dermal Chemotaxis + FGF20/BMP Lateral Inhibition behind a Geodesic EDA Competence Wave on a Curved Monge-Patch Skin Surface with Density-Threshold Tract Boundaries (Painter, Ho & Headon 2018; Ho et al. 2019; Bausch et al. 2003)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_019.disclination_charge" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_019.euler_disclination_charge" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Isochrone Row-Count Dislocation Lemma on a Curved Tract" ;
    dct:description "Proves that where the surface metric stretches successive isochrones by at least one period (limb-bud flank), the later row must carry an extra primordium — a terminating row = 5-7 dislocation. isochrone_row_count_check() verifies the lemma on the simulated isochrones (0 violations) and reports the number of row-count jumps on flat vs curved surfaces. | Variables: L_1, L_2: arc lengths of successive geodesic isochrones of the EDA competence wave; λ: inhibitory-disk spacing (λ_y); ⌊L/λ⌋: number of primordia a row can hold" ;
    dct:source "Ho et al. (2019) PLoS Biol. 17:e3000132 Fig 1B, 4C-D; Bausch et al. (2003) Science 299:1716-1718" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2018-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal.py#L795-L842>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_019_avian_feather_bud_hexagonal.lean#L147-L156> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def isochrone_primordium_count (L lam : Nat) : Nat :=
  L / lam
theorem isochrone_row_count_dislocation (L1 L2 lam : Nat)
    (h_pos : 0 < lam) (h_longer : L1 + lam ≤ L2) :
    isochrone_primordium_count L1 lam + 1 ≤ isochrone_primordium_count L2 lam := by
  simp only [isochrone_primordium_count]
  have h1 : (L1 + lam) / lam = L1 / lam + 1 := Nat.add_div_right L1 h_pos
  have h2 : (L1 + lam) / lam ≤ L2 / lam := Nat.div_le_div_right h_longer
  omega
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "L_1 + λ ≤ L_2  ⟹  ⌊L_1 / λ⌋ + 1 ≤ ⌊L_2 / λ⌋" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2017.10.026>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1081160>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.018341>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.3000132>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.3000448> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Keller-Segel Dermal Chemotaxis + FGF20/BMP Lateral Inhibition behind a Geodesic EDA Competence Wave on a Curved Monge-Patch Skin Surface with Density-Threshold Tract Boundaries (Painter, Ho & Headon 2018; Ho et al. 2019; Bausch et al. 2003)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_019.isochrone_primordium_count" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_019.isochrone_row_count_dislocation" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-6> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Monge-Patch Metric Determinant (well-posedness of the surface Laplace-Beltrami operator)" ;
    dct:description "Proves the induced metric of the trunk-and-limb-bud surface is never degenerate (det g ≥ 1), so sqrt(det g), g^{ij} and the Laplace-Beltrami / surface-chemotaxis operators implemented in build_embryo_trunk_surface() and surface_div_grad() are well defined everywhere. | Variables: h(u, v): skin height field of the Monge patch; p = h_u², q = h_v², s = h_u h_v: metric coefficients" ;
    dct:source "Painter, Ho & Headon (2018) J. Theor. Biol. 437:225-238 (PDE system); standard differential geometry of Monge patches" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2018-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal.py#L314-L399>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_019_avian_feather_bud_hexagonal.lean#L169-L182> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def monge_metric_det (p q s_sq : Nat) : Nat :=
  (1 + p) * (1 + q) - s_sq
theorem monge_metric_determinant (p q s_sq : Nat) (h_cross : s_sq = p * q) :
    monge_metric_det p q s_sq = 1 + p + q ∧ 1 ≤ monge_metric_det p q s_sq := by
  subst h_cross
  have h_expand : (1 + p) * (1 + q) = 1 + p + q + p * q := by
    simp [Nat.add_mul, Nat.mul_add, Nat.one_mul, Nat.mul_one]
    omega
  constructor
  · simp only [monge_metric_det]
    omega
  · simp only [monge_metric_det]
    omega
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "g = [[1 + h_u², h_u h_v], [h_u h_v, 1 + h_v²]],  det g = (1 + p)(1 + q) - s² = 1 + p + q ≥ 1  (p = h_u², q = h_v², s² = p q)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2017.10.026>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1081160>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.018341>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.3000132>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.3000448> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Keller-Segel Dermal Chemotaxis + FGF20/BMP Lateral Inhibition behind a Geodesic EDA Competence Wave on a Curved Monge-Patch Skin Surface with Density-Threshold Tract Boundaries (Painter, Ho & Headon 2018; Ho et al. 2019; Bausch et al. 2003)" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_019.monge_metric_det" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_019.monge_metric_determinant" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Painter, Ho & Headon (2018) Keller-Segel / FGF20 Dermal Chemotactic Instability vs. Scaleless (sc/sc) Stability" ;
    dct:description "Proves that supercritical FGF20 chemotaxis (χ > χ_c) drives spontaneous dermal mesenchymal condensation (det_KS < 0), whereas FGF20 loss in the scaleless (sc/sc) mutant or Latrunculin motility blockade (χ = 0) guarantees uniform dermal stability (det_KS > 0). In the Pass 3 code the same χ_c gates the nucleation rule (chi < CHI_CRITICAL => no primordia). | Variables: n(x,t): dermal mesenchymal cell density; c(x,t): FGF20 chemoattractant; χ: chemotactic sensitivity; D_n, D_c: diffusivities; q = k^2: squared spatial wavenumber" ;
    dct:source "Painter, Ho & Headon (2018) J. Theor. Biol. 437:225-238 Section 2-3; Ho et al. (2019) PLoS Biol. 17(2):e3000132 Fig 1C, S5 Fig" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2018-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal.py#L167-L229>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_019_avian_feather_bud_hexagonal.lean#L29-L48> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def keller_segel_fgf20_det (D_n r_n D_c mu_c chi n_0 f_c q : Int) : Int :=
  (D_n * q + r_n) * (D_c * q + mu_c) - chi * n_0 * f_c * q
def scaleless_neg_trace (D_n D_c r_n mu_c q : Nat) : Nat :=
  (D_n + D_c) * q + (r_n + 1) + (mu_c + 1)
def scaleless_pos_det (Dq_prod D_n_mu D_c_r r_pos : Nat) : Nat :=
  Dq_prod + D_n_mu + D_c_r + (r_pos + 1)
theorem keller_segel_fgf20_chemotactic_instability (D_n D_c r_n mu_c q Dq_prod D_n_mu D_c_r r_pos : Nat) :
    scaleless_neg_trace D_n D_c r_n mu_c q ≥ 2 ∧
    scaleless_pos_det Dq_prod D_n_mu D_c_r r_pos ≥ r_pos + 1 ∧
    keller_segel_fgf20_det 1 1 1 2 0 1 3 1 = 6 ∧
    keller_segel_fgf20_det 1 1 1 2 1 1 3 1 = 3 ∧
    keller_segel_fgf20_det 1 1 1 2 4 1 3 1 = -6 := by
  refine ⟨?_, ?_, by decide, by decide, by decide⟩
  · simp [scaleless_neg_trace]; omega
  · simp [scaleless_pos_det]
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "det_KS(q) = (D_n q + r_n)(D_c q + μ_c) - χ n_0 f_c q < 0  (χ > χ_c),   det_KS(q)|_{χ=0} = (D_n q + r_n)(D_c q + μ_c) > 0  ∀ q > 0" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2017.10.026>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1081160>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.018341>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.3000132>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.3000448> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Keller-Segel Dermal Chemotaxis + FGF20/BMP Lateral Inhibition behind a Geodesic EDA Competence Wave on a Curved Monge-Patch Skin Surface with Density-Threshold Tract Boundaries (Painter, Ho & Headon 2018; Ho et al. 2019; Bausch et al. 2003)" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_019.keller_segel_fgf20_det" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_019.keller_segel_fgf20_chemotactic_instability" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Equilateral Row-to-Row Half-Phase Offset & 6-Equidistant Nearest-Neighbor Theorem (Ho et al. 2019 Fig 3B lattice)" ;
    dct:description "Proves that when lateral inhibition pins each successive mediolateral row at half-period offset Δy = λ_y / 2 and spacing Δx = (√3/2) λ_y, all 6 nearest neighbours lie at identical distance λ_y (60° hexagonal array). Used by the primary-row / inhibitory-disk nucleation geometry and by the flat-sheet P_6 = 1.0 control. | Variables: λ_y: longitudinal intra-row feather bud spacing; Δy = λ_y / 2: inhibitor-pinned half-period phase offset; Δx: mediolateral inter-row spacing" ;
    dct:source "Ho et al. (2019) PLoS Biol. 17:e3000132 Fig 3B, Fig 2A; Painter, Ho & Headon (2018) J. Theor. Biol. 437:225-238 Fig 5" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2018-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal.py#L231-L312>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_019_avian_feather_bud_hexagonal.lean#L63-L74> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def scaled_inter_row_diag_dist_sq (dx_sq ly_sq : Int) : Int :=
  4 * dx_sq + ly_sq
def scaled_intra_row_dist_sq (ly_sq : Int) : Int :=
  4 * ly_sq
theorem hexagonal_row_offset_equidistance (dx_sq ly_sq : Int)
    (h_hex : 4 * dx_sq = 3 * ly_sq) :
    scaled_inter_row_diag_dist_sq dx_sq ly_sq = scaled_intra_row_dist_sq ly_sq := by
  simp [scaled_inter_row_diag_dist_sq, scaled_intra_row_dist_sq]
  omega
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "d_diag^2 = (Δx)^2 + (λ_y / 2)^2 = λ_y^2  ⟺  4(Δx)^2 = 3 λ_y^2  ⟺  Δx = (√3 / 2) λ_y ≈ 0.8660 λ_y" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2017.10.026>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1081160>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.018341>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.3000132>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.3000448> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Keller-Segel Dermal Chemotaxis + FGF20/BMP Lateral Inhibition behind a Geodesic EDA Competence Wave on a Curved Monge-Patch Skin Surface with Density-Threshold Tract Boundaries (Painter, Ho & Headon 2018; Ho et al. 2019; Bausch et al. 2003)" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_019.scaled_inter_row_diag_dist_sq" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_019.hexagonal_row_offset_equidistance" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Ho et al. (2019) & Bailleul et al. (2019) Traveling Competence Wave Hexagonal Fidelity Enhancement Theorem" ;
    dct:description "Proves that sequential row-by-row competence propagation achieves strictly higher hexagonal fidelity P_6 than simultaneous whole-tract competence (Ho 2019 Fig 2D: ~75 % vs ~50 % six-sided Voronoi cells, control vs Latrunculin-paused explants). Pass 3 corrects the attribution: the simultaneous regime is the Latrunculin-pause/release experiment, not Fc-chEDA1. | Variables: v_w: mediolateral EDA competence wave speed; P_6: percentage of 6-coordinated Voronoi polygons; d_min: intrinsic defect floor; d_gain: simultaneous-nucleation grain-boundary defect penalty" ;
    dct:source "Ho et al. (2019) PLoS Biol. 17(2):e3000132 Fig 2B-D, Fig 4; Bailleul et al. (2019) PLoS Biol. 17(10):e3000448" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2018-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal.py#L844-L912>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_019_avian_feather_bud_hexagonal.lean#L89-L103> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def hexagonal_p6_opt_pct (d_min : Nat) : Nat :=
  100 - d_min
def hexagonal_p6_simul_pct (d_min d_gain : Nat) : Nat :=
  100 - (d_min + (d_gain + 1))
theorem traveling_wave_hexagonal_fidelity_advantage (d_min d_gain : Nat)
    (h_bound : d_min + (d_gain + 1) ≤ 100) :
    hexagonal_p6_opt_pct d_min > hexagonal_p6_simul_pct d_min d_gain ∧
    hexagonal_p6_opt_pct 8 = 92 ∧
    hexagonal_p6_simul_pct 8 41 = 50 := by
  refine ⟨?_, by decide, by decide⟩
  simp [hexagonal_p6_opt_pct, hexagonal_p6_simul_pct]
  omega
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "P_6(v_opt) = 100 - d_min > P_6(v → ∞) = 100 - (d_min + d_gain)  (d_gain ≥ 1);   P_6(v_opt) = 92% > P_6(v → ∞) = 50%" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2017.10.026>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1081160>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.018341>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.3000132>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.3000448> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Keller-Segel Dermal Chemotaxis + FGF20/BMP Lateral Inhibition behind a Geodesic EDA Competence Wave on a Curved Monge-Patch Skin Surface with Density-Threshold Tract Boundaries (Painter, Ho & Headon 2018; Ho et al. 2019; Bausch et al. 2003)" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_019.hexagonal_p6_opt_pct" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_019.traveling_wave_hexagonal_fidelity_advantage" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Euler / Gauss-Bonnet Disclination Charge of a Closed Triangulated Primordium Lattice (Bausch et al. 2003)" ;
    dct:description "Proves that Gaussian curvature forces 5-/7-coordinated defects into the hexagonal feather lattice independent of the primordium positions: on the curved limb-bud flanks the humeral and femoral tracts must dislocate. Checked numerically by sphere_topological_charge_check() (charge 12 on a Fibonacci sphere) and used by curvature_defect_analysis() to localise 5-7 pairs where |K| > K_thr. | Variables: V, E, F: vertices (primordia), edges, triangular faces of the Delaunay lattice; z_i: coordination number; χ: Euler characteristic; n_5, n_7: five- and seven-coordinated primordia" ;
    dct:source "Bausch et al. (2003) Science 299(5613):1716-1718; Ho et al. (2019) PLoS Biol. 17:e3000132 Fig 1B (tracts on the curved trunk and limbs)" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2018-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal.py#L437-L546>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_019_avian_feather_bud_hexagonal.lean#L119-L133> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def disclination_charge (V sum_z : Int) : Int :=
  6 * V - sum_z
theorem euler_disclination_charge (V E F sum_z : Int)
    (h_faces : 3 * F = 2 * E) (h_degrees : sum_z = 2 * E) :
    disclination_charge V sum_z = 6 * (V - E + F) := by
  simp [disclination_charge]
  omega
theorem sphere_pentagon_excess (n5 n6 n7 E F : Int)
    (h_faces : 3 * F = 2 * E)
    (h_degrees : 5 * n5 + 6 * n6 + 7 * n7 = 2 * E)
    (h_euler : (n5 + n6 + n7) - E + F = 2) :
    n5 - n7 = 12 := by
  omega
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "Σ_i (6 - z_i) = 6V - Σ z_i = 6(V - E + F) = 6χ   (3F = 2E, Σ z_i = 2E);   sphere: n_5 - n_7 = 12" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2017.10.026>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1081160>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.018341>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.3000132>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.3000448> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Keller-Segel Dermal Chemotaxis + FGF20/BMP Lateral Inhibition behind a Geodesic EDA Competence Wave on a Curved Monge-Patch Skin Surface with Density-Threshold Tract Boundaries (Painter, Ho & Headon 2018; Ho et al. 2019; Bausch et al. 2003)" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_019.disclination_charge" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_019.euler_disclination_charge" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Isochrone Row-Count Dislocation Lemma on a Curved Tract" ;
    dct:description "Proves that where the surface metric stretches successive isochrones by at least one period (limb-bud flank), the later row must carry an extra primordium — a terminating row = 5-7 dislocation. isochrone_row_count_check() verifies the lemma on the simulated isochrones (0 violations) and reports the number of row-count jumps on flat vs curved surfaces. | Variables: L_1, L_2: arc lengths of successive geodesic isochrones of the EDA competence wave; λ: inhibitory-disk spacing (λ_y); ⌊L/λ⌋: number of primordia a row can hold" ;
    dct:source "Ho et al. (2019) PLoS Biol. 17:e3000132 Fig 1B, 4C-D; Bausch et al. (2003) Science 299:1716-1718" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2018-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal.py#L795-L842>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_019_avian_feather_bud_hexagonal.lean#L147-L156> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def isochrone_primordium_count (L lam : Nat) : Nat :=
  L / lam
theorem isochrone_row_count_dislocation (L1 L2 lam : Nat)
    (h_pos : 0 < lam) (h_longer : L1 + lam ≤ L2) :
    isochrone_primordium_count L1 lam + 1 ≤ isochrone_primordium_count L2 lam := by
  simp only [isochrone_primordium_count]
  have h1 : (L1 + lam) / lam = L1 / lam + 1 := Nat.add_div_right L1 h_pos
  have h2 : (L1 + lam) / lam ≤ L2 / lam := Nat.div_le_div_right h_longer
  omega
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "L_1 + λ ≤ L_2  ⟹  ⌊L_1 / λ⌋ + 1 ≤ ⌊L_2 / λ⌋" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2017.10.026>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1081160>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.018341>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.3000132>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.3000448> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Keller-Segel Dermal Chemotaxis + FGF20/BMP Lateral Inhibition behind a Geodesic EDA Competence Wave on a Curved Monge-Patch Skin Surface with Density-Threshold Tract Boundaries (Painter, Ho & Headon 2018; Ho et al. 2019; Bausch et al. 2003)" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_019.isochrone_primordium_count" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_019.isochrone_row_count_dislocation" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal-6> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Monge-Patch Metric Determinant (well-posedness of the surface Laplace-Beltrami operator)" ;
    dct:description "Proves the induced metric of the trunk-and-limb-bud surface is never degenerate (det g ≥ 1), so sqrt(det g), g^{ij} and the Laplace-Beltrami / surface-chemotaxis operators implemented in build_embryo_trunk_surface() and surface_div_grad() are well defined everywhere. | Variables: h(u, v): skin height field of the Monge patch; p = h_u², q = h_v², s = h_u h_v: metric coefficients" ;
    dct:source "Painter, Ho & Headon (2018) J. Theor. Biol. 437:225-238 (PDE system); standard differential geometry of Monge patches" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2018-glimm-avian-feather-bud-hexagonal.py#L314-L399>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_019_avian_feather_bud_hexagonal.lean#L169-L182> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def monge_metric_det (p q s_sq : Nat) : Nat :=
  (1 + p) * (1 + q) - s_sq
theorem monge_metric_determinant (p q s_sq : Nat) (h_cross : s_sq = p * q) :
    monge_metric_det p q s_sq = 1 + p + q ∧ 1 ≤ monge_metric_det p q s_sq := by
  subst h_cross
  have h_expand : (1 + p) * (1 + q) = 1 + p + q + p * q := by
    simp [Nat.add_mul, Nat.mul_add, Nat.one_mul, Nat.mul_one]
    omega
  constructor
  · simp only [monge_metric_det]
    omega
  · simp only [monge_metric_det]
    omega
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "g = [[1 + h_u², h_u h_v], [h_u h_v, 1 + h_v²]],  det g = (1 + p)(1 + q) - s² = 1 + p + q ≥ 1  (p = h_u², q = h_v², s² = p q)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2017.10.026>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1081160>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1242/dev.018341>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.3000132>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pbio.3000448> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Keller-Segel Dermal Chemotaxis + FGF20/BMP Lateral Inhibition behind a Geodesic EDA Competence Wave on a Curved Monge-Patch Skin Surface with Density-Threshold Tract Boundaries (Painter, Ho & Headon 2018; Ho et al. 2019; Bausch et al. 2003)" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_019.monge_metric_det" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_019.monge_metric_determinant" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

